# Full Bore: "If that creature was cast for its warp cost" (CR 702.185a). Another keyword's alternative cost is not warp's:
# Bot1 attacks with Memnite on turn 3, then casts Spider-Man, Web-Slinger for its web-slinging cost {W} (Mox Pearl),
# returning the tapped Memnite, and Full Bore on it (Mox Ruby): a 6/5 with neither trample nor haste.

[Bot1 Deck]
Memnite
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Spider-Man, Web-Slinger
Full Bore
Mountain x2
Mountain x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x24

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spider-Man, Web-Slinger.Cast(Ability: Web-slinging)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Full Bore.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Spider-Man, Web-Slinger)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.End]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Spider-Man, Web-Slinger.Power = 6
? Bot1.Battlefield.Spider-Man, Web-Slinger.Keywords = (absent)

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Memnite; Mountain; Mountain; Mountain
Bot1.Graveyard = Full Bore
